---
description: Use temporary variables and Vala string interpolation (@"") for SQL instead of .printf().
alwaysApply: true
---

# SQL string interpolation

Build multi-line SQL queries with Vala string templates (`@" ... $(var) ... "`), computing any conditional clauses in temporary variables beforehand.

Do not append `.printf(...)` to SQL strings unless there is a compelling reason (such as a `printf` format specifier that interpolation cannot express).

```vala
// Wrong. Trailing .printf() hides what each placeholder maps to.
query.selectQuery("""
	SELECT
		%s
	WHERE
		%s
	""".printf(columns, agent_id > 0 ?
		"system_info.agent_id = %d".printf(agent_id) :
		"system_info.agent_id IN (SELECT id FROM agent)"), rows);

// Right. Temporary variable (using `if` instead of a string ternary) + inline Vala interpolation.
var where = "system_info.agent_id = " + agent_id.to_string();
if (agent_id < 1) {
	where = "system_info.agent_id IN (SELECT id FROM agent)";
}
query.selectQuery(@"
	SELECT
		$(columns)
	WHERE
		$(where)
	", rows);
```
